   ***** MDOS Version MDOS56  (grm) *****
    

A new version of the Mach DOS software is now available.  This version
contains several new features.  The most interesting of which is a
secondary loader that loads the Mach DOS monitor code into high
memory.  What this means, is that the mdos program itself is no longer
three meg, but is about 170K.

Sup service for Mach DOS is now available from CMU.  To get this
release via sup use the sup collection below:

mdos host=x29.mach.cs.cmu.edu hostbase=/i386 base=<HERE> crypt=mdos

Edit <HERE> to be the directory where you want the code to be placed.

The build procedure is outlined in mdos.install.{ps,doc} in the
src/setup directory.  Remember that you must be running Mach 3.0
release MK73 or later!

NOTE:  IF THE MDOS.MON FILE INSTALLED IN LIB IS AROUND 16MEG, YOU
ARE USING THE WRONG LOADER!!!  SUP YOUR APPLICATION BINARIES AGAIN!!

New features:
--- --------

The loader describe above.

The Interrupt Vector Table override code was rewritten to occur after
COMMAND.COM executes instead of after the first keyboard event.  This
means that the pause after your first keystroke is gone.

