   ***** MDOS Version MDOS58  (grm) *****
    


Mach DOS release MDOS58 is now available via sup from CMU.  This
release has several new features along with some bug fixes.  The main
things in this release are the new SuperVGA support and the timer fix
(fixes sound problems and slow graphics).

Again, for those who are new to the mdos mailing list, in order to sup
the Mach DOS software collection you should add the following line to
your supfile:

mdos host=x29.mach.cs.cmu.edu hostbase=/i386 base=<HERE> crypt=mdos

Edit <HERE> to be the directory where you want the code to be placed.

NOTE: the crypt is "mdos" and is NOT site specific.

The build procedure is outlined in mdos.install.{ps,doc} in the
src/setup directory.  Remember that you must be running Mach 3.0
release MK73 or later!

New features:
--- --------

Provided framework for extensible SuperVGA code.  Provided the Tseng
Lab's ET4000 support as a model.  Now you can pause or exit Mach DOS
from the ET4000's high resolution modes like 800x600x256 or
1024x768x256 now.  Before this would lead to a VERY confused VGA card.

Bug fixes:
--- -----

Fixed the timer bug introduced with MK73.  Timeouts on ports round up
to the nearest 10 milliseconds now, so the timer code in bios_misc.c
had to compensate by subtracting 10 milliseconds from the timeout
value.  This fixes the slow music and slow graphics in DOS
applications that demand timer interrupts with small intervals.

Corrected the single drive installation bug that was introduced in
MDOS56.  This bug made it impossible for machines with only one
floppy drive from accessing drive B: in mdos.  This has been fixed.

